          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "SP 90 SW                  CHARTRIDGE          CHARTRIDGE                                               (north side) 5/23                                          Old Zac's Cottage and                                               Raymond's Cottage 22.12.58 GV                                            II Small house, now divided into two cottages.  Early C17, timber frame, red brick infill, old tiled roof with half-hipped gables.  2-storeys, projecting cross wing on left with jettied upper floor.  One 3-light casement to ground floor, 2-light above.  Right hand part had two doors, two 2-light and one 1-light casement to ground floor, two 2- light casements on first floor and a later gabled dormer in the centre.  Interior: Front room of cross wing has chamfered ceiling joists, central room has large inglenook with chamfered beam; heavy timber framing exposed including curved windbraces to roof. Listing NGR: SP9372603560"
    }
  ],
